From 877555720c20bfc076f0eb9bdea39197565c099d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xie Fei <fei.cn.xie@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:11:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(kv_transfer): recover the aligned KV backing base for
 hybrid Mooncake registration

Hybrid KV cache views can begin after Mamba padding, page padding, or a
non-zero descriptor offset inside the shared arena, so a view address is
not the 2 MiB aligned backing base. The hybrid registration helper used
the smallest view address as the registration base and refused to
register when it was unaligned, which aborted engine startup on both P/D
hosts of a DeepSeek-V4 deployment:

  RuntimeError: Tensor start addr <addr> is not aligned to 2 MiB.

DeepSeek-V4 stacks the SFA indexer layers of one group into one shared
arena and vLLM offsets the second spec bucket by
`indexer_page_bytes * num_blocks` (16640 * num_blocks here), which is not
2 MiB aligned, so no launch flag can avoid it.

Route the hybrid case through the storage-based helper already used by
the Mamba path. It recovers the aligned base from the backing storage,
falls back to registering the real per-storage ranges when no single
aligned backing covers a descriptor, and merges duplicate regions. This
also stops registering `descriptor.size` bytes starting from a shifted
view, which would have overrun the allocation whenever the offset
happened to be 2 MiB aligned. Drop the then-unused
`_get_registered_kv_tensor_buffers_hybrid` and log the registered region
count and total size for field diagnosis.

Add a regression test covering a shared arena whose views start at a
non-zero descriptor offset, including the remainder observed on the
prefill node.

Signed-off-by: Xie Fei <fei.cn.xie@gmail.com>
